    "body": "## Purpose\n\nThe NVIDIA V1 Attention steps (H100 and B200) were split into 2 fixed pytest shards (`--shard-id` / `--num-shards`, `parallelism: 2`), and each shard still takes 46–51 min. This turns each into one plain `pytest -v -s v1/attention` step with `automatic_shard: true`, the same as #60492, #60662, #60757 and #60858.\n\nThe pipeline generator then plans the shards at bootstrap from main's per-file timings. It splits the two big MLA files by test function. Planned shards on current timings:\n\n| Step | Shards | Estimated minutes per shard |\n|---|---|---|\n| `v1-attention-h100-mi300` | 6 | 15.9 each |\n| `v1-attention-b200` | 6 | 16.4 ×5, 19.1 |\n\nThe AMD mirrors (MI300, MI355 DPX) are unchanged. They keep their fixed pytest shards, because `automatic_shard` covers NVIDIA steps only, so the shard args and `parallelism: 2` move into the mirror config.\n\n## Test Plan\n\nBuildkite build https://buildkite.com/vllm/ci/builds/94185, running only these two steps. I'll add wall time, GPU time and test counts against main here.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
